resume: Thinking of man in relation to history is to admit that diversity is at the heart of the process of humanization. Africa has experienced a situation of dehumanization based on the idea that Africans have not participated in the elaboration of the historical process. The analysis starts from the struggles of liberation and identity claim known in the black diaspora, and the affirmation of a humanity among Africans through the exercise of philosophical activity.
